  "preamble": "The transformation of the voiceless velar plosive /k/ to the voiced velar plosive /g/ is a common phonetic shift, driven by voicing assimilation or lenition, often intervocalically or after nasals. Oghuz Turkic voiced word-initial *k- before front vowels (Proto-Turkic *kün > Turkish gün 'day'). Imbabura Kichwa voices *k after a consonant (*ʈʂunka > ʧuŋga 'ten'). In Western Armenian Classical կ /k/ became [ɡ] (կին 'woman' [ɡin]); Eastern Armenian keeps [k].",
  "phoneticEffects": "Voicing, Lenition, Assimilation",
